  <p class="note">Each happens once (the user's rule). The inspector asks about a machine you really serviced and watches your real team job, and the creature's weaning uses tuning, so both draw on what you've done. Loss of Power needs Nell aboard that week as an everyday guest with her parent (the crew designer's guests).</p>
</section>

<section id="q">
  <h2>Questions for the user (with my recommendations)</h2>
  <ol>
    <li><b>Loss of Power's group:</b> Brennan, Nell and Commander Vance? <i>Recommended: yes (Holt instead of Vance would be funnier, but Vance's story is the heart of it).</i></li>
    <li><b>Getting you into the lift:</b> someone calls "Hold the doors!" when you're near the spine at 10:00, so you're nearly always inside; if you're far away, you help from outside. <i>Recommended: yes.</i></li>
    <li><b>The creature's name:</b> a crew vote with your suggestion in it ("Sprat" leads). <i>Recommended: yes, as with the garden pet.</i></li>
    <li><b>The inspector's findings:</b> read out to everyone in a meeting, plus a Mail. <i>Recommended: yes, short and kind.</i></li>
    <li><b>Halden:</b> leave it a mystery, a seed for the story pillar (Pillar 7) to pick up. <i>Recommended: yes.</i></li>
  </ol>
